      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Executive Summary\nThis summary outlines critical compliance requirements under the Data Integrity Protocol v4.2, ensuring full adherence to new security standards.\n\n# Encryption Standards\nAll user data must be encrypted at rest using AES-256 to guarantee strong data protection across all systems.\n\n# Record Retention Policy\nAccess logs must be strictly retained for a minimum of seven years to satisfy full audit trail obligations.\n\n# Breach Reporting Procedures\nAny data breach must be reported to the oversight committee within 24 hours to minimize potential impact.\n\n# Vulnerability Management\nPeriodic vulnerability scans are mandatory every quarter to proactively identify and mitigate security risks.\n\n# Vendor Compliance\nAll third-party vendors must sign a Data Processing Agreement (DPA) before receiving any Personally Identifiable Information.",
